WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:17.577
Izzie and her grandmother walked into cooking class together.

2
00:00:17.597 --> 00:00:21.939
"This will be fun, Isabel!"

3
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.240
Grandma said.

4
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:27.182
"Ugh," Izzie thought.

5
00:00:27.202 --> 00:00:29.744
"She called me Isabel again!"

6
00:00:30.996 --> 00:00:34.399
Izzie wanted to tell Grandma that she didn't like being called Isabel.

7
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.442
But she didn't want to hurt Grandma's feelings.

8
00:00:39.544 --> 00:00:41.145
The boys were washing their hands.

9
00:00:41.165 --> 00:00:44.108
"Hi, Bobby and Jason!"

10
00:00:44.448 --> 00:00:45.049
Izzie said.

11
00:00:45.069 --> 00:00:47.151
"This is my grandma."

12
00:00:47.171 --> 00:00:50.193
"Hi," the boys said together.

13
00:00:50.213 --> 00:00:54.677
"Our friend Nina isn't here today," Jason said.

14
00:00:54.697 --> 00:00:57.400
"Her family is visiting Korea."

15
00:00:59.204 --> 00:01:03.145
"I take a senior cooking class with Chef," Grandma said.

16
00:01:03.165 --> 00:01:07.407
"I missed a class, so I'm doing a make-up with you."

17
00:01:07.427 --> 00:01:10.828
"Cool!" Bobby said.

18
00:01:12.588 --> 00:01:13.888
Chef greeted everyone.

19
00:01:13.908 --> 00:01:17.750
"Today we're making Rainbow Stir-Fry."

20
00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.611
Grandma looked at the recipe on the screen.

21
00:01:21.631 --> 00:01:26.776
"Why is it called 'rainbow' stir-fry?"

22
00:01:26.796 --> 00:01:30.158
"Chef says we should eat the rainbow,'" Izzie said.

23
00:01:30.178 --> 00:01:33.959
"That means eating lots of colorful fruits and vegetables.

24
00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.560
They're full of nutrients."

25
00:01:38.261 --> 00:01:39.922
Grandma pinched Izzie's cheeks.

26
00:01:41.262 --> 00:01:46.725
"My little granddaughter is so smart!"

27
00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:49.926
"Yikes!" Izzie whispered to the boys.

28
00:01:49.946 --> 00:01:53.668
"This is so embarrassing."

29
00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:58.710
"My grandfather treats me like a baby too," Jason whispered.

30
00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:04.192
"Last Hanukkah he gave me a huge stuffed animal."

31
00:02:04.212 --> 00:02:11.014
"Grandparents want us to stay little forever," Bobby whispered.

32
00:02:13.756 --> 00:02:15.716
Everyone got busy chopping vegetables.

33
00:02:16.897 --> 00:02:18.397
Grandma cut up red cabbage.

34
00:02:19.358 --> 00:02:22.819
Jason chopped broccoli, and Bobby cut the bell pepper.

35
00:02:23.339 --> 00:02:24.460
Izzie chopped carrots.

36
00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.021
Chef heated oil in a wok.

37
00:02:28.041 --> 00:02:33.143
"For stir-fries, we don't add all the vegetables at once.

38
00:02:34.283 --> 00:02:36.684
We start with those that take longest to cook."

39
00:02:38.405 --> 00:02:39.445
He looked at the class.

40
00:02:39.465 --> 00:02:41.846
"What should I cook first?"

41
00:02:41.866 --> 00:02:45.948
"Broccoli?" Bobby asked.

42
00:02:47.048 --> 00:02:48.529
"Nope," Chef said.

43
00:02:48.549 --> 00:02:52.811
"I think carrots take longer," Izzie said.

44
00:02:52.831 --> 00:02:58.798
"Yes! Carrots first, then broccoli," Chef said.

45
00:02:58.818 --> 00:03:02.581
"Bell pepper next," Bobby said.

46
00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:05.924
"Then cabbage," Jason said.

47
00:03:07.746 --> 00:03:08.486
Chef nodded.

48
00:03:08.506 --> 00:03:12.430
"Bobby, please open that can of baby corn.

49
00:03:13.471 --> 00:03:15.432
It cooks quickly, so we'll add it last."

50
00:03:16.553 --> 00:03:17.514
He turned to Izzie.

51
00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:20.597
"Please get the chicken from the refrigerator.

52
00:03:21.758 --> 00:03:24.000
Your grandmother can cut it into thin strips."

53
00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:28.981
Grandma chuckled.

54
00:03:32.763 --> 00:03:37.747
Isabel was little, she called the refrigerator a foodrater.

55
00:03:38.688 --> 00:03:39.728
Isn't that cute?"

56
00:03:40.929 --> 00:03:42.250
"Not again!"

57
00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.492
Izzie thought as she got the chicken.

58
00:03:44.512 --> 00:03:48.314
"Another embarrassing comment!"

59
00:03:52.617 --> 00:03:56.040
While Grandma sliced the chicken, the kids began making the sauce.

60
00:03:58.076 --> 00:03:59.136
Izzie chopped ginger.

61
00:04:00.217 --> 00:04:03.057
Jason chopped garlic, and Bobby squeezed the lemon.

62
00:04:04.518 --> 00:04:08.079
They added those ingredients to vegetable oil, soy sauce, and honey.

63
00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.941
surprised we're making a healthy dish," Grandma said.

64
00:04:15.961 --> 00:04:19.502
"I thought we'd make something that kids like.

65
00:04:20.402 --> 00:04:21.522
Like hot dogs."

66
00:04:23.343 --> 00:04:26.364
"I love eating healthy foods and trying new things!"

67
00:04:26.864 --> 00:04:27.784
Izzie burst out.

68
00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.641
Grandma looked surprised.

69
00:04:31.741 --> 00:04:34.302
"Really?" "Yes!"

70
00:04:34.982 --> 00:04:35.603
Izzie said.

71
00:04:35.623 --> 00:04:40.505
"This class is the same as my adult classes," Chef said.

72
00:04:40.525 --> 00:04:45.207
"We learn all about food," Bobby said.

73
00:04:45.227 --> 00:04:49.468
"And how to do things ourselves," Izzie said.

74
00:04:51.029 --> 00:04:53.030
Grandma nodded but didn't say anything.

75
00:04:55.531 --> 00:04:57.792
Jason moved the cooked vegetables to a bowl.

76
00:05:00.956 --> 00:05:02.837
Izzie helped Chef stir-fry the chicken.

77
00:05:06.659 --> 00:05:09.781
When it was cooked, Bobby put the vegetables back in the wok.

78
00:05:11.422 --> 00:05:12.803
Grandma added the sauce.

79
00:05:14.444 --> 00:05:16.225
All the ingredients simmered together.

80
00:05:19.727 --> 00:05:22.088
Chef served the stir-fry over cooked rice.

81
00:05:22.108 --> 00:05:24.469
"Now we can eat!"

82
00:05:30.528 --> 00:05:31.911
Grandma smiled at Izzie.

83
00:05:32.592 --> 00:05:36.860
"You're growing up fast, Isabel, er Izzie."

84
00:05:38.002 --> 00:05:38.743
Izzie grinned.

85
00:05:38.763 --> 00:05:41.808
"I'm glad you came today, Grandma."
